          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Rules"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.181,
            0.808,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is a two player game. Each player has 1 pawn. Both players start at 0. Players can reach either – 50 or + 50 to win but need not decide or fix this before or during play."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.249,
            0.808,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each player rolls two dice at a time. One dice has numbers from + 1 to + 6 and the other dice has numbers from – 1 to – 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.294,
            0.809,
            0.385
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After each roll of the two dice, the player can add or subtract them in any order and then move the steps that indicate the result. A positive result means moving towards + 50 and a negative result means moving towards – 50."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
